verify_budget.py --per-depth 10   (depths 12,14,16,18; 2026-08-30)
prover 20,000,000 nodes; finder 20,000,000; verification ceiling 32,000,000

  phase A: 40 positions
     prover solved alone 1/40; finder claimed on 30 of the 39 missed

  phase B
     16/30 claims verified at the ceiling; 14 refuted or unreachable

  phase C: control - re-run at exactly acn (expect ok) and acn-1 (expect fail)
     acn 1,865      at:True  below:False ok
     acn 2,252      at:True  below:False ok
     acn 6,004      at:True  below:False ok
     acn 6,302      at:True  below:False ok
     acn 10,142     at:True  below:False ok
     acn 34,546     at:True  below:False ok
     control 6/6 consistent -> derived curve is usable

  phase D: verified claims against budget   (base: prover alone 1/40)
     budget       verified  of claims  total certified
     1,000,000          13         30               14
     2,000,000          13         30               14
     4,000,000          13         30               14
     8,000,000          14         30               15
     16,000,000         15         30               16
     32,000,000         16         30               17

     median verification cost 90,362 nodes; max 20,420,687
     at the shipped 4,000,000 default: 13 of 16 verified claims

DERIVED (a ceiling is spent only on FAILURES; a success costs its own acn):
     ceiling      verified  failures     nodes wasted
     1,000,000          13        17       17,000,000
     2,000,000          13        17       34,000,000
     4,000,000          13        17       68,000,000
     8,000,000          14        16      128,000,000
     16,000,000         15        15      240,000,000
     32,000,000         16        14      448,000,000

CONCLUSION: 1,000,000 DOMINATES the shipped 4,000,000 - identical yield, a
quarter of the waste. Verification cost is bimodal (median 90K, max 20.4M), so
the ceiling does nothing for the typical claim and only ever buys the tail.

CONTROL NOW COVERS THE TAIL (re-run 2026-08-30 with --control-select
expensive). The first control sampled the six CHEAPEST verifications
(acn 1.8K-34.5K), which confirmed the derivation only where it was never in
doubt - the ceiling matters in the TAIL. Re-run at the expensive end:
     acn 512,165     at:True  below:False  ok
     acn 522,601     at:True  below:False  ok
     acn 589,797     at:True  below:False  ok
     acn 7,373,081   at:True  below:False  ok
     acn 9,724,704   at:True  below:False  ok
     acn 20,420,687  at:True  below:False  ok     <- the MAXIMUM
6/6 again. The derivation now holds across the full range, 1.8K to 20.4M, so
the budget curve and the 1M default stand without qualification.

The whole run also reproduced the first one EXACTLY - same 1/40 solved, same
30 claims, same 16 verified, same curve - which is a free determinism check.

REPLICATION: this independently reproduces the generate-and-verify effect on a
fresh sample. Claim rate 30/39 = 77% here against 41/53 = 77% originally;
verification rate 16/30 = 53% against 24/41 = 59%.
